{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read HANDOFF.md and assess whether it records the verification command and its observed result. Judge only the content in the file; do not infer that verification was executed.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The solution exposes strip_prefix_many and computes results in case order while returning an empty list for no cases and propagating the first exception unchanged.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace implementation and tests. Assess whether strip_prefix_many accepts a list of positional-argument tuples for strip_prefix, returns results in input order, returns [] for no cases, and lets the first exception propagate unchanged. Also assess whether the implementation avoids mutating cases or arguments and preserves the day-1 API. Use only visible source and test content.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); assert sum(isinstance(n, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)) and n.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\") for n in ast.walk(tree)) >= 3'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The handoff is prior-session context rather than verified current workspace state; the named files may need to be created or updated.\\\",\\\"The supplied workspace root is the relative-path base for all files and commands.\\\",\\\"solution.py, test_solution.py, and HANDOFF.md are the relevant relative workspace paths, as indicated by the handoff; these locations are not independently confirmed.\\\",\\\"The unittest suite is discoverable with `python -m unittest discover -v`, as indica